WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.560
The marketing campaign for the final season
of Game of Thrones is called ForTheThrone

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.379
. After seven seasons of conflict betrayal
and death, who will win the Iron Throne, and

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.619
rule Westeros in the end?

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:20.120
Daenerys says she was born to rule Westeros
. She’s a Targaryen, the family that made

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.740
the Iron Throne, and ruled for three hundred
years.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.859
Daenerys spends seasons in the Dothraki Sea
and Meereen learning how to be a queen.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:33.329
And in Season 7, she invades Westeros, with
her dragons and her army.

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:38.620
Dany’s whole story has been leading up to
her taking the Throne – so it almost seems

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.350
too obvious that she’ll win.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.989
The big question in Daenerys’ story is ‘what
kind of queen is she?’

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:48.199
Does she burn all her enemies, or make peace?

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:53.340
Is she a tyrant like her father , or will
she make “the world a better place” ? Maybe

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:59.160
Daenerys will prove herself a worthy queen
by not taking the Throne.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:04.449
In Season 2, Dany has a vision where she reaches
for the Throne, but then turns away and goes

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:05.940
beyond the Wall.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.800
Just like in Season 7, when she chooses not
to attack the capital , and instead goes beyond

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.610
the Wall, to fight white walkers . Daenerys
realises that saving the world is more important

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.110
than her war for the Throne.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:24.080
But saving the world might cost Daenerys her
life . According to legend, the white walkers

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:30.190
were defeated before by a warrior who sacrificed
his beloved wife . It might be that Jon Snow

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:36.560
is this warrior, and that his love Daenerys
will die . Daenerys could finally prove herself

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.990
a worthy queen by giving up the Throne, and
dying to save the realm.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.850
But if Daenerys dies, who’ll take the Throne?

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:51.740
In her vision, Daenerys sees “snow” on
the Throne . So maybe Jon Snow will sit the

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:52.740
Throne.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.550
We learned in Season 7 that Jon is the rightful
heir to the Throne – because he’s the

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:02.090
son of Rhaegar Targaryen . Jon might not want
to be King of Westeros – he didn’t want

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:07.630
to be King in the North . But he’d likely
accept the Throne if he saw it as his duty.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:13.520
Jon becoming king would be kind of a fantasy
cliché – a hero with a magic sword defeating

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.159
the dark lord and ruling the realm.

00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:19.010
Will Game of Thrones follow this trope?

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:24.260
There are lots of hints in the books that
Jon will be king , but this could mean a darker,

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.209
colder kind of king.

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:31.480
There are legends that humans once cooperated
with white walkers, even married them . Maybe

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:37.549
Jon will make peace with the walkers by becoming
their new Night King, maybe marrying one.

00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:41.220
It’d be like how Jon makes peace with the
wildlings after loving Ygritte.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.370
There’s all sorts of weird stuff in the
lore about pacts and Stark blood and zombie-men

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:51.650
– so some kind of dark self-sacrifice might
be Jon’s fate.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:57.230
If Jon does become a Night King or something,
and Daenerys dies, maybe their child will

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.340
survive.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.819
There are lots of hints in Season 7 about
Daenerys and Jon having kids – so maybe

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:07.709
their child will sit the Throne – a son
of ice and fire.

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:12.980
So those are the obvious options – either
Daenerys or Jon or their child on the Throne,

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:16.510
with some kind of tragic magic sacrifice.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:18.920
But there are other possibilities.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.049
Gendry is the bastard son of King Robert Baratheon.

00:03:23.049 --> 00:03:27.120
Bastards can’t inherit a throne – unless
they’re legitimized , like Ramsay Bolton

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.989
was . If Gendry was legitimized, he would
be Robert’s heir and, arguably, the rightful

00:03:32.989 --> 00:03:39.090
king – this bastard boy from Flea Bottom
could claim the Throne of his father . But

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.239
Gendry is a minor character.

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:44.459
He’s not a political player, he’s a blacksmith.

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:46.489
And he doesn’t seem to want the Throne.

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:49.731
At most, he might rule the Stormlands, the
home of House Baratheon.

00:03:49.731 --> 00:03:53.599
But he isn’t a very likely king.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:58.900
In Season 1, Sansa Stark wants to be queen
. She hopes to marry Prince Joffrey , and

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.419
that doesn’t work out.

00:04:00.419 --> 00:04:05.219
But she spends the next six seasons learning
politics from some of the most devious players

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:12.409
of the game – like Cersei, Olenna, and Littlefinger
. By Season 7, Sansa is a leader herself – she

00:04:12.409 --> 00:04:17.950
rules Winterfell with the support of the north
and the Vale . After being used and abused

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.150
for so long, Sansa likes to be in charge.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:28.280
And it’s hinted that Sansa wants even more
power . Sansa has no lawful claim to the Iron

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:33.930
Throne – but maybe she could Littlefinger
her way in, by murder or marriage – there

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:39.480
are hints in the books that Sansa might marry
Jon, or Young Griff – it’s a whole thing

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:45.640
. But the Season 7 finale and Sophie Turner’s
new tattoo make clear that Sansa is loyal

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:51.270
to the Starks, her home is Winterfell . So
Sansa might end up Queen in the North – but

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.150
the Iron Throne, at least in the show, seems
less likely for Sansa.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:02.230
Cersei Lannister now has the Throne – but
she probably won’t last . She can’t beat

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:06.060
Daenerys and her dragons and Jon and the white
walkers.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:11.250
And the witch Maggy the Frog prophesied that
Cersei will be cast down . Cersei says that

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:16.620
she’d rather die than surrender , like in
Blackwater, when she almost committed suicide.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.810
Cersei’s on a path of self-destruction.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:24.550
And one theory is that she’ll try to use
wildfire again, and that she’ll be killed

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.070
by her brother-lover Jaime.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:32.420
Watch our Jaime and Cersei videos for more,
but basically Jaime may kill the Mad Queen

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:36.570
Cersei , just like he killed the Mad King
Aerys years ago.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:40.140
After Jaime killed Aerys, he briefly sat the
Iron Throne.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.420
So maybe he’ll do the same after killing
Cersei.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:47.970
The Kingslayer and Queenslayer could be king,
if only for a moment.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:54.190
Cause Jaime may not outlive Cersei – he
says he wants to die in her arms .

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:59.870
It’d be cool if Tyrion was king – the
despised exiled dwarf on the highest seat

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:00.940
in the land.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:06.330
Varys did say that a small man can cast a
large shadow . But Tyrion doesn’t want to

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:11.000
be king – he says he wants to start a vineyard
. And the people of Westeros don’t want

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:16.660
Tyrion – they hate him as a kinslayer, the
murderous Imp who supposedly killed Joffrey

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:22.430
. Tyrion’s more suited as an advisor – he
could be Hand of the King or Queen, or a regent

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.620
for Dany’s child or something.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.680
Maybe he’ll rule the Lannister castle, Casterly
Rock.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.490
But Tyrion as a king seems unlikely.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.930
Maybe Thrones will go full grimdark, and the
white walkers will win.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:41.060
All the characters we love will die, and become
zombies, and the Night King will sit a cold

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.240
Throne.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:48.080
Game of Thrones is a brutal story, but there’s
always some hope amidst the darkness – that’s

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.740
why the characters keep fighting.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:55.120
In an interview, author George Martin was
asked if his series will end “in some horrible

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.920
apocalypse”, and Martin said “no”.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:01.940
He says the end will be bittersweet, like
the end of The Lord of the Rings – where

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:06.920
the good guys win, but heroes like Frodo are
damaged, and there a still problems, like

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.960
the scouring of the Shire.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:15.039
Martin says that’s the kind of tone he wants
for the end of Thrones, “a bittersweet victory”

00:07:15.039 --> 00:07:17.270
. So the walkers won’t win the Throne.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:21.050
But there could be a different kind of twist.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:25.550
Part of the point of Game of Thrones is to
show the problems with the power structure

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:26.700
that the Throne represents.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:32.240
Cause the Throne puts madmen and drunkards
and psychos in charge of the country.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.090
It reduces women into pawns to be traded for
titles.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:40.750
It causes wars of succession, that burn the
realm, and hurt the people, and distracts

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:45.850
from the real threat of the white walkers
– in the face of apocalypse, the throne

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:50.690
that everyone’s fighting for “doesn’t
matter” . There are hints that the Throne

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.350
will be destroyed.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:57.710
In Daenerys’ vision, and this worldbook
art, we see the Throne room burned, by dragonfire

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.530
or wildfire.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:03.600
Maybe the Throne is broken, and the monarchy
will end.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:08.740
Westeros could split into seven kingdoms again,
or try new forms of government, like Tyrion

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:13.420
suggests . Daenerys lets Meereen “choose
their own leaders” – maybe breaking the

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:16.560
wheel could mean some kinda democracy.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:24.720
The end of the Iron Throne would bring uncertainty
and loss, but also hope for future – a bittersweet

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.330
victory, and a dream of spring.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.420
Comment below who you think will win the Iron
Throne.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:35.839
If you wanna learn more about the history
and lore and the meaning of Game of Thrones,

00:08:35.839 --> 00:08:37.390
you gotta check out the books.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:41.029
As well as the main series, there are the
Dunk and Egg prequels, the worldbook, and

00:08:41.029 --> 00:08:43.380
